/ref 1079 #uuid "579ac401-6a63-5a61-82b5-87d55aa593a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462487 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462488 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462489 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106897" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $10?$\n- **I.** ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$\n- **II.** ${\\text{M}}_{5}(R)$, the vector space of all $5\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n- **III.** ${R}^{10}$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c2f74bb-ddf4-5d4c-b244-ad5b6a694598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243975 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11\\ne 10.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(\\text{R}))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{5}(R))={5}^{2}=25\\ne 10.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{10})=10.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256787 #edb/ref 1080 "-11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256787 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256787 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0086e1d8-f0ee-53c6-8443-35f56170d9d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
